{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Clutch, backlash, and rotational sources",
  "exampleId": "block-rotational-sources",
  "description": "The clutch closes at 0.5 s and drags its 1 kg·m² load up to the 100 rad/s the speed source reached at 0.1 s, then locks. The backlash leaves the driven inertia standing still until the sine-driven source has taken up half the 0.1 rad gap, at 0.04 s. A torque source of 0.5 N·m drives an inertia through a spring and a damper in parallel; the inertia has 0.05 N·m·s of damping to the housing, so it settles at 10 rad/s. A constant 0.4 N·m accelerates a 0.002 kg·m² inertia against 0.05 N·m of load torque until the torque step raises the load to 0.4 N·m at 0.45 s; then it coasts down against its 0.001 N·m·s damping.",
  "duration": 2,
  "revision": 0,
